{
    "background_story": "Felipe was a free-spirited musician who lived for the open road. With his guitar and a backpack, he traveled from town to town, sharing his music with anyone who would listen. He had no fixed address, no steady income, and no desire to settle down. Felipe's itinerant lifestyle allowed him to soak up the rhythms and stories of the places he visited, which he would then weave into his songs. From the jazz clubs of New Orleans to the folk festivals of Rio, Felipe's music was a reflection of his wanderlust and love of adventure. Despite the unpredictability of his life, he was always drawn to the next horizon, the next melody, and the next stranger who might become a friend. Felipe's music was a testament to the beauty of living life on the move.",
